About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A Hybrid working model

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. This team will sit onsite with our client in their Hoboken office 3 days per week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.

Purpose of the Role &nbsp;

The Content Effectiveness Hub (CEH) is a Client dedicated tech-enabled, human-led team that scales high-performing omnichannel content across social and digital assets for Global Personal Care brands in North America. As a Content Producer, you will be a key WPP Production resource embedded in the Hub, working as part of an integrated team with Strategy, Creative &amp; Media. &nbsp;

You will oversee the production of modular content at scale: building, versioning and adapting assets from approved hero creative, using modular templates, toolkits, data feeds, motion tooling and AI-enabled workflows. You will focus on Adapt and Modify tier work. &nbsp;

You will partner with Strategy, Creative and Content Operations to bring a production lens to modular design thinking, so concepts are built for scale. You will ensure every asset is on-brief, on-spec, on-brand and ready to deploy, while continually improving speed, quality and efficiency. &nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

Modular production delivery &nbsp;

• Direct and coordinate production resources, including motion designers, designers and AI-tool operators, to deliver against the asset production briefs and timelines. &nbsp;

• Support production execution of modular Adapt and Modify briefs across display and social, working from the production brief provided by Strategists and the workflow board and timelines set by Content Ops. &nbsp;

• Flag template or toolkit issues and improvement needs back to template and toolkit owners. &nbsp;

• Apply the provided naming taxonomy to all assets and manage versioning matrices, so deliverables are traceable, accurate and ready for hand-off to the Content Ops for delivery and media activation. &nbsp;

Integrated team partnership &nbsp;

• Partner upstream with Strategists, Creative and Content Ops to review briefs and asset grids for production feasibility and confirm the modular production approach. &nbsp;

• Advise on modular design thinking for production, including how templates, components and layouts should be structured for efficient versioning, feasibility, formats, timing and cost, so creative concepts are designed to scale. &nbsp;

• Partner with WPP Media teams, so specs, platform requirements and deployment plans are met. &nbsp;

• Collaborate with the E2E Content Deployment Planner and Creative Adaptation roles to keep the content flow from brief to live execution seamless. &nbsp;

